  "body": "\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI am writing a game that I use Matrix as my chat protocol. As each user logs in I want the game to be able to attach some data from the user to the room, and for that data to be accessible by every other user.\r\nI do this so that when a user hosts a game, it attached some json about the game that the other players can then join.\r\n\r\nI almost got there with the .../state/{custom_event_type}/{state_key} (where the state key is the user id) API, but that only works for the user who created the room. Other uses get a forbidden response.\r\n\r\nI suppose the quick solution would be to allow any user to have permission to write a state key based on their user id or some room permission to set certain events as publicly read/writable.\r\n",
